.TH SYS_PROC_THREADS 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_threads \- list thread IDs for a process
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_threads(pid_t " pid ", tid_t *" tids ", size_t *" count ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_proc_threads ()
returns thread IDs associated with process
.IR pid .
The caller supplies an output array in
.I tids
and an in/out element count in
.IR *count .
.PP
If
.I pid
is 0, the current process is implied.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.
On error, a negative value is returned by the current implementation.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOSYS
Current kernel implementation is a stub and returns not implemented.
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid pointers or invalid count pointer semantics.
.SH NOTES
This syscall number is wired in native dispatch, but the current kernel handler
is a stub in `sys/kern/syscall.c`.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_proc_info (2),
.BR sys_proc_list (2),
.BR thr_self (2)
